/*
 * Zephyr's rpi_5 takes zephyr,sram from the SoC's sram0
 * (dts/arm64/broadcom/bcm2712.dtsi: 512 KiB at 0x200000, two address cells).
 * This image carries the V3D's 96 MiB carve-out, the compiler's 2 MiB
 * scratch, the 96 MiB C heap (prj.conf) and glmark2's ~9.4 MB of data files,
 * so it gets 288 MiB from 0x200000, to 0x12200000, as the Pi 4's glmark2
 * does (boards/rpi_4b.overlay; an estimate there too). The range stays below
 * 4 GiB, so the V3D's page table entries and the mailbox's buffer address fit
 * (docs/notes/pre-study-rpi5.md, U10). Whether the firmware leaves all of it
 * to the kernel is not read in this tree: the first board run settles it
 * (docs/notes/rpi5-deqp-glmark2.md, section 4). Zephyr's own mailbox driver
 * (mbox0) stays disabled, as bcm2712.dtsi has it: the board layer's
 * rpi_mbox.c owns the mailbox.
 */
&sram0 {
	reg = <0x0 0x200000 0x12000000>;
};
